          "sizeGB": 41,
          "notes": "Audio-driven lip sync on MiniMax H3. Up to 9 reference images in one shot, and H3 syncs the person at the microphone rather than everyone in frame.\n\nHOW THE AUDIO WORKS: H3 uses reference audio that matches the shot length. A reference longer than the clip is not used, and the model generates its own vocal instead - which it then lip-syncs convincingly, so it can look correct while ignoring your track. This preset trims automatically to the shot length, so that does not happen. Verified by correlating the output's audio against the source: an untrimmed 213 s track scored 0.006, the same track trimmed scored 0.947 at exactly the requested offset.\n\nUse START OFFSET to choose which part of a song the shot syncs to - no need to cut audio files by hand.\n\nMEASURED on a 12 GB card at 864x480 with 6 references:\n  5 s  / 6 steps  -> 150 s, correlation 0.947\n  10 s / 6 steps  -> 420 s, correlation 0.948 (sync holds at double length)\n  5 s  / 10 steps -> 225 s, correlation 0.950 - no better sync and no visible picture gain, so leave steps at 6.\nRender time scales worse than linearly with duration (2x length cost 2.8x time). A 10 s take still beats two 5 s takes plus a cut you did not want.\n\nMATCH YOUR AUDIO LENGTH TO THE SHOT. If the track is shorter than the duration you asked for, H3 syncs correctly until the audio runs out and then invents the remainder - the tail comes back as convincing but meaningless singing. With the duration defaulting to 10 s, a 5 s upload gives you 5 good seconds and 5 invented ones. Either upload a longer track (a whole song is fine - it gets trimmed) or lower the duration to fit the audio."
